OL,3,GNEWSACalls to save tree near Paul
OL,4,AMcCartney home
OL,5,
OL,6,FResidents have urged a housing
OL,7,Fassociation to explore every option to
OL,8,Fsave a mature tree which has been in
OL,9,Ftheir community for generations.
OL,11,FThe tree on Hurstlyn Road in Allerton
OL,12,Fstands about 100 yards from Forthlin
OL,13,FRoad, where Sir Paul McCartney grew up,
OL,14,Fand residents said Beatles fans
OL,15,Fvisiting the area often photograph it.
OL,17,FTorus, a housing association operating
OL,18,Facross the North West, said independent
OL,19,Finspections had found the tree had a
OL,20,Frotting core and dead wood, and advised
OL,21,Fthat it should be felled.
OL,23,APub: 29-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
